": 284, "end": 350, "text": "Heard, publisher of the newspaper now called The Arizona Republic."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0342-3ab07137bb75:d01", "start": 351, "end": 481, "text": "“Phoenix Sky Line Soars,” proclaimed the newspaper’s front page when the Security Building opened eight months later in July 1918."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0342-3ab07137bb75:d01", "start": 482, "end": 577, "text": "The structure was built with reinforced concrete with a focus on modern design and engineering."}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0342-3ab07137bb75:d02", "start": 0, "end": 71, "text": "The Security Improvement Company when the building was erected in 1905."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0342-3ab07137bb75:d02", "start": 72, "end": 201, "text": "In the 1950s, the famous penthouse was added, where Phoenix mover and shaker Walter Bimson, president of Valley Bank, once lived."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0342-3ab07137bb75:d02", "start": 202, "end": 296, "text": "The Security Building was added to the National Register of Historic Places in September 1985."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0342-3ab07137bb75:d02", "start": 297, "end": 333, "text": "Grace Lutheran Church (1928) 1124 N."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0342-3ab07137bb75:d02", "start": 334, "end": 343, "text": "Third St."}, "D3S6": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0342-3ab07137bb75:d02", "start": 344, "end": 470, "text": "| The building is constructed in the Gothic Revival architectural style and represents the European Traditional property type."}, "D3S7": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0342-3ab07137bb75:d02", "start": 471, "end": 602, "text": "Important decorative elements include crenulated parapets, a dominant rose window, buttressed pilasters, stained glass, and lancet."}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0342-3ab07137bb75